course: dictionary
lesson: 8487
title: Words about desert birds
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You do not need to know every word to understand a text. Read the words around a new word, because they leave clues. «Male sandgrouse soak their belly feathers at a waterhole and fly many kilometres back to their chicks.» The sentence says the sandgrouse has feathers and flies, so it must be a bird.
explain: The words waterhole and wet feathers are clues too. The chicks drink from the wet feathers, so the birds must be in a place where water is hard to find.
explain: Check your guess by putting it into the sentence. Does «Male birds soak their belly feathers at a waterhole» still make sense? Yes, so you are on the right track. When context is not enough, use a dictionary.
fact: A sandgrouse is a bird of dry, sandy places in Africa and Asia.
fact: Sandgrouse are related to pigeons.
fact: Their sandy-coloured feathers hide them on the ground.
fact: «Sandgrouse» is a noun. You can say a flock of sandgrouse.
exercise: What is a sandgrouse? | A fish that swims in rivers | *A bird of dry, sandy places in Africa and Asia | A tree with sandy roots | A kind of desert cactus
exercise: Why are sandgrouse hard to see on the ground? | They are very large and loud | They live in deep water | *Their sandy-coloured feathers hide them | They fly only at night
exercise: Find and copy one word that means a group of sandgrouse. | waterhole | feathers | desert | *flock
test: In «Male sandgrouse soak their belly feathers at a waterhole», what does waterhole probably mean? | *A pool of water in a dry place | A place to sleep at night | A rainy cloud | A hole dug in a rock for a tree
test: Why do the males fly back to their chicks? | To sing for their mates | *To carry water to their chicks in the desert | To find a new flock | To eat seeds from the trees
exam: Where do sandgrouse live? | A snowy mountain | A green rainforest | *A dry, sandy desert | A deep ocean
